  allows teams of six to work together  other game modes include a racing  version of good old battle royale where  undoubtedly receiving this game because  it did so poorly in terms of sales but  the reviews all say it's a good arcade  racer definitely worth a download right  over on the ps3 is Sterry den a pixel  art scrolling shooter the soundtrack in  particular is damn impressive but in  terms of mechanics if you play the art  type series you know  what to expect here use power-ups to  take down your enemies and then take  down a boss at the end of each section  rinse repeat nothing to write home about  but if you like that sort of thing  starey Danny's perfect for you next we  have steins gate yet another visual  novel on ps3 I feel like we talked about  these quite a lot this is all about  changing the pasts to create new story  arcs you don't really play steins gate  you experience it as the genre of visual  novel suggests there's a great deal of  reading here but if you pay attention  you'll be rewarded with branching  options to drastically mix up things for  the characters you love and the ones you  hate - okay over to the Vita the first  game which is playable on the ps4  iconoclasts this is a superb little  action platformer with a gorgeous art  style and is another game released this  calendar year gameplay involves fighting  and exploring as you'd expect but the  puzzles really help break up the  repetition and can be challenging in  later game the game puts you in the  mindset of preparing for boss fights and  allows you to practice with a range of  mailing and other weapons in terms of  story your unliveable mechanic named  robin who decides to take on a sinister  religious group why not I suppose sadly  there's not enough review scores to help  us here so we'll have to move on instead  and finally game sticks is a beast  papers please it's such a damn great  game does it involve shooting people no  does it have the greatest graphics ever  no this is gonna be hard to sell but  papers please puts you in the shoes of  an immigrations officer attempting to  decide who can enter the country and who  is sent away it's a game that teaches  empathy and I could not recommend it any  higher you must decide if you will take  a bribe and maybe use that money to help  your family but what if that person who  came in is here for nefarious reasons  and everything is traced back to you  there's so many small heart racing  decisions to make here if you have a  Vita I beg you to play it so there we  have it  eight games for December what do you  think okay I know it's a bad month in  general but keep in mind Sony wants us  buying games around Christmas time so we  tend to receive lesser games at this  time of year but in terms of 2018 as a  whole this has been great for PS Plus  please let me know your thoughts I  imagine from PlayStation granade it's  been a pleasure  I'll see you  time
 

